{"content":"Implemented the depfile/dyndep rebuild fix.\n\n### Changes\n- Updated `DependencyScan::RecomputeNodeDirty` in `src/graph.cc` to:\n  - Visit all inputs first.\n  - Only then evaluate their dirty and readiness states.\n- This ensures a later input loading a dyndep file can retroactively attach a producer and mark an earlier depfile-discovered input dirty before the consumer’s rebuild decision is made.\n- Added `BuildTest.DyndepReadyDiscoverOutputAndDepfileInput` in `src/build_test.cc`, reproducing the dependency ordering from the reported issue and asserting both producer and consumer run in the same build.\n\n### Verification\nFinal source review confirmed the change is narrowly scoped and preserves order-only dependency behavior and mtime selection.\n\nAutomated tests could not run because `python3 configure.py --bootstrap` failed immediately: the host has no usable Xcode command-line tools (`xcode-select: No developer tools were found`). Consequently, the focused regression test remains unexecuted in this environment.","type":"text"}
